        "body": "Thanks for the work put into this! Found a few things to address regarding install. I'll try installing and testing again once those are amended.\r\n\r\nSome notes\r\n- There are install instructions we can simplify/remove.\r\n- I know we briefly talked about who the intended users are. We can discuss more with @jstonge if needed. I think the user class for py-allotax are researchers who can code but who are not developers. In this case, we need to make instructions for dev tools easier and provide more scaffolding—or make sure the stuff that can be abstracted away *is* in the docker image and package install... to that end, we'd definitely want to get to the pip install stage--I am admittedly unclear on what install steps here would be abtracted away when we do that. Currently, the install steps feel like it’s gone up in technical background needed.\r\n- Please have a researcher who codes test out the new install instructions on this branch. I had Calla Beauregard and Tessa Lawler (lab members) both test out prior iterations. ",
