          "type": "User",
          "user_view_type": "public",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "body": "## Description\r\nAdds functionality to easily build a .whl file for distribution of the package. Once this is finished, we should look into publishing the .whl to https://pypi.org/. That way, we can just have people `pip install py-allotax`, no cloning needed.\r\n### Added\r\n- Dockerfile that builds package for distribution\r\n- Make project a PDM project\r\n- build.sh script to install npm and node, build docker image, and retrieve built package\r\n- test in tests/ to make sure the plot generation works.\r\n\r\n### Changed\r\n- Moved example data to the top-level of project (so its not a part of package when distributed\r\n- Restructured src directory for distribution (mostly moving things inside the py_allotax directory)\r\n- change line in generate_svg_minimum that calls generate_svg to find the script and index.html where-ever the package is installed\r\n- change line in generate_svg to parse arg for index.html path\r\n- package.json and package-lock.json into src/py_allotax for easy use upon distribution\r\n- moved example_charts to highest level directory\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n1. run \r\n   ```pdm sync```\r\n   and then:\r\n   ```pdm run pytest```\r\n   to run generation test.\r\n2. Follow the instructions in the README.md to build and install the package in a consumer project.",
