          "message": "ARM64: configs: alpha/beta/flash/mh2lm: enable CONFIG_PROC_CMDLINE_APPEND_ANDROID_FORCE_NORMAL_BOOT\n\nChange-Id: Ie83607e8b4337cc97e29425e4114d43cb4e3423b\nSigned-off-by: Han Sol Jin <hansol@hansol.ca>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/3d4eec05d0afdd7dddaf0ad5f9065d5154e3333c"
        },
        {
          "sha": "dc8a7d20756b345621169026495e0593bb772b6a",
          "author": {
            "email": "genesis45.ppc@gmail.com",
            "name": "AShiningRay"
          },
          "message": "techpack: audio: es9218p: add centralized sysfs and left/right balance control\n\nChange-Id: Ib5f703651f94a5fbb8b2416c0e59d49c5cf5996e",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/dc8a7d20756b345621169026495e0593bb772b6a"
        },
        {
          "sha": "6dcab9db9f968ead9a91942643510825d09845fc",
          "author": {
            "email": "markusornik@gmail.com",
            "name": "SGCMarkus"
          },
          "message": "techpack: audio: es9218p: add ess filter sysfs\n\nChange-Id: Ic61560e179c047239025032a632e302135f64334",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/6dcab9db9f968ead9a91942643510825d09845fc"
        },
        {
          "sha": "59a5dd55a6a2b2b3327b14e01b4fd7da875bb2aa",
          "author": {
            "email": "genesis45.ppc@gmail.com",
            "name": "AShiningRay"
          },
          "message": "techpack: audio: es9218p: Introduce a customizable ESS filter, fix return values\n\nThis commit introduces support for a customizable filter that can\nbe adjusted by users through the revamped DAC Panel, and also\nreworks many return statements when the DAC is in an invalid state\nor couldn't allocate enough memory.\n\nChange-Id: I2ce790eb42387b7b3c803c6c18b73e673842ffc4",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/59a5dd55a6a2b2b3327b14e01b4fd7da875bb2aa"
        },
        {
          "sha": "b7bd7f609113f3fe09fb31464734f271faec05c8",
          "author": {
            "email": "genesis45.ppc@gmail.com",
            "name": "AShiningRay"
          },
          "message": "techpack: audio: es9218p: Only update custom data on the custom filter slot\n\nPreviously an incorrect configuration on the dac panel could cause\nthe driver to override coefficients, shape and symmetry on the stock\nfilters. By hard-coding the slot to that of the custom filter, we\ncan impede that from happening since there is only one custom filter\nslot.\n\nChange-Id: Iad43305bdc36c26e0f94db8d2c436018e67e1670",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/b7bd7f609113f3fe09fb31464734f271faec05c8"
        },
        {
          "sha": "dcef718ee738bb8a2c91783e23201aaefc1d1a31",
          "author": {
            "email": "genesis45.ppc@gmail.com",
            "name": "AShiningRay"
          },
          "message": "techpack: audio: es9218p: Apply current filter on every ESS playback call\n\nWith the current dac panel implementation, the panel has no way\nof keeping track of media playback states and that led to filter\nsetups being lost whenever a media seek or any other task that\nrestarts playback were done.\n\nSince the ess kernel driver DOES keep track of those things, let's\napply the last used filter every time it detects media playback,\nit's far cleaner of a solution and AVC is already made persistent\nbetween playbacks in that same way.\n\nChange-Id: I9769da8c962c292330c1f8089847e9921243150a",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/dcef718ee738bb8a2c91783e23201aaefc1d1a31"
        },
        {
          "sha": "ee1b90ea7270339436887e6559c35842442f9127",
          "author": {
            "email": "hansol@hansol.ca",
            "name": "Han Sol Jin"
          },
          "message": "techpack: audio: es9218p: adjust master volume in set_forced_ess_filter()\n\nLGE adjusts this in `mute_work_function`, which is called when the HAL\ntriggers a fade in/out for the filter change.\n\nFollow suit in the sysfs-based implementation, minus the fading.\n\nChange-Id: I7339b1016fb4b5cb2f214d4a95c330b5e3d7e705",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/ee1b90ea7270339436887e6559c35842442f9127"
        },
        {
          "sha": "c74b3f5d95958436784270d71949874927bb6438",
          "author": {
            "email": "hansol@hansol.ca",
            "name": "Han Sol Jin"
          },
          "message": "treewide: fix -Wstrict-prototypes error in LGE changes\n\nChange-Id: I15526a31cfe7c9460f462b18bf74638fd6cd242c\nSigned-off-by: Han Sol Jin <hansol@hansol.ca>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/c74b3f5d95958436784270d71949874927bb6438"
        },
        {
          "sha": "be26cef3ae8ac929b44bd23283a3348b96b797b9",
          "author": {
            "email": "jb@essential.com",
            "name": "Jean-Baptiste Théou"
          },
          "message": "techpack: audio: tfa98xx: add error translation routine\n\nChange-Id: I4d1d428f0306bbe6bb25d8beab8a74307aaeadf7",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/be26cef3ae8ac929b44bd23283a3348b96b797b9"
        },
        {
          "sha": "87432db1c0d33f72295862a4f57ddd9c49268e32",
          "author": {
            "email": "emanuelghub@gmail.com",
            "name": "EmanuelCN"
          },
          "message": "techpack: audio: es9218p: Fix memory leak in set_forced_ess_custom_filter\n\nChange-Id: I23ae316a0599830f5b8b1ae312bc46b7dcb6e10c",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/87432db1c0d33f72295862a4f57ddd9c49268e32"
        },
        {
          "sha": "0d1f2e99c600258033af0cc6242b014b05dec649",
          "author": {
            "email": "hansol@hansol.ca",
            "name": "Han Sol Jin"
          },
          "message": "input: touchscreen: s3618: wake the panel when longpress is enabled\n\nCurrently this device is blanking the display after doze, because\nwithout doing so, it causes the screen to never show the AOD UI.\n\nOn mh2lm in particular, this causes weird issues with the under-display\nfingerprint sensor; the touch panel is set to deep sleep mode, so the\npanel never reports to userspace that the fingerprint area has been\npressed in order to unlock the phone.\n\nThis is supposed to be handled in `s3618_lpwg_mode()` which is run on\n`s3618_suspend()`, but unfortunately userspace is trying to enable the\n`longpress` sysfs far too late and the panel ends up going to deep\nsleep; the check in `s3618_lpwg_longpress_enable()` when triggering the\nsysfs thus fails.\n\nWith the preface out of the way, we can just run `s3618_lpwg()`, which\nin turn runs `s3618_lpwg_mode()`, the latter of which will check that\nlongpress is enabled and re-wake the screen.\n\nChange-Id: I7f4c82a3d5d3011986a29e3cc76a1697441f5da6\nSigned-off-by: Han Sol Jin <hansol@hansol.ca>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lge-qcom-dev/android_kernel_lge_sm8150/commits/0d1f2e99c600258033af0cc6242b014b05dec649"
        }
      ]
    },
