        "title": "Git Bash: gpg hangs on most commands",
        "user": {
          "login": "Zxilly",
          "id": 31370133,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMxMzcwMTMz",
          "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31370133?v=4",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Zxilly",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/Zxilly",
          "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Zxilly/followers",
          "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Zxilly/following{/other_user}",
          "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Zxilly/gists{/gist_id}",
          "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Zxilly/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
          "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Zxilly/subscriptions",
          "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Zxilly/orgs",
          "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Zxilly/repos",
          "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Zxilly/events{/privacy}",
          "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Zxilly/received_events",
          "type": "User",
          "user_view_type": "public",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "labels": [],
        "state": "open",
        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 0,
        "created_at": "2025-01-01T15:12:01Z",
        "updated_at": "2025-01-01T15:12:01Z",
        "closed_at": null,
        "author_association": "NONE",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": " - [x] I was not able to find an [open](https://github.com/git-for-windows/git/issues?q=is%3Aopen) or [closed](https://github.com/git-for-windows/git/issues?q=is%3Aclosed) issue matching what I'm seeing\r\n\r\n### Setup\r\n\r\n - Which version of Git for Windows are you using? Is it 32-bit or 64-bit?\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ git --version --build-options\r\n\r\ngit version 2.48.0.rc1.windows.1\r\ncpu: x86_64\r\nbuilt from commit: 5d54b0dddfd3a18a649edccdaf0f428b6b2ec507\r\nsizeof-long: 4\r\nsizeof-size_t: 8\r\nshell-path: D:/git-sdk-64-build-installers/usr/bin/sh\r\nfeature: fsmonitor--daemon\r\nlibcurl: 8.11.1\r\nOpenSSL: OpenSSL 3.2.3 3 Sep 2024\r\nzlib: 1.3.1\r\n```\r\n\r\n - Which version of Windows are you running? Vista, 7, 8, 10? Is it 32-bit or 64-bit?\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ cmd.exe /c ver\r\n\r\nMicrosoft Windows [Version 10.0.26100.2605]\r\n(c) Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.\r\n```\r\n\r\n - What options did you set as part of the installation? Or did you choose the\r\n   defaults?\r\n\r\n```\r\n# One of the following:\r\n> type \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\etc\\install-options.txt\"\r\n> type \"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Git\\etc\\install-options.txt\"\r\n> type \"%USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Git\\etc\\install-options.txt\"\r\n> type \"$env:USERPROFILE\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Git\\etc\\install-options.txt\"\r\n$ cat /etc/install-options.txt\r\n\r\nEditor Option: VisualStudioCode\r\nCustom Editor Path:\r\nDefault Branch Option:\r\nPath Option: Cmd\r\nSSH Option: OpenSSH\r\nTortoise Option: false\r\nCURL Option: OpenSSL\r\nCRLF Option: LFOnly\r\nBash Terminal Option: ConHost\r\nGit Pull Behavior Option: Rebase\r\nUse Credential Manager: Enabled\r\nPerformance Tweaks FSCache: Enabled\r\nEnable Symlinks: Enabled\r\nEnable FSMonitor: Disabled\r\n```\r\n\r\n - Any other interesting things about your environment that might be related\r\n   to the issue you're seeing?\r\n\r\nThis is a new issue after upgrading to git 2.47.1.\r\n\r\n### Details\r\n\r\n - Which terminal/shell are you running Git from? e.g Bash/CMD/PowerShell/other\r\n\r\nPowerShell\r\n\r\n - What commands did you run to trigger this issue? If you can provide a\r\n   [Minimal, Complete, and Verifiable example](http://stackoverflow.com/help/mcve)\r\n   this will help us understand the issue.\r\n\r\n```\r\ngpg --gen-key -vvvv --debug-all\r\n```\r\n - What did you expect to occur after running these commands?\r\n\r\nGot a new key\r\n\r\n - What actually happened instead?\r\n\r\nThe process hang forever. The `gpg-agent` receives the handshake but seems do nothing.\r\n\r\n```\r\ngpg output\r\n$ gpg --gen-key -vvvv --debug-all\r\ngpg: reading options from '[cmdline]'\r\ngpg: reading options from '/c/Users/zxilly/.gnupg/common.conf'\r\ngpg (GnuPG) 2.4.5-unknown; Copyright (C) 2024 g10 Code GmbH\r\nThis is free software: you are free to change and redistribute it.\r\nThere is NO WARRANTY, to the extent permitted by law.\r\n\r\ngpg: using character set 'utf-8'\r\ngpg: enabled debug flags: packet mpi crypto filter iobuf memory cache memstat trust hashing ipc clock lookup extprog\r\ngpg: enabled compatibility flags:\r\nNote: Use \"gpg --full-generate-key\" for a full featured key generation dialog.\r\n\r\nGnuPG needs to construct a user ID to identify your key.\r\n\r\nReal name: A\r\nEmail address:\r\nYou selected this USER-ID:\r\n    \"A\"\r\n\r\nChange (N)ame, (E)mail, or (O)kay/(Q)uit? O\r\nWe need to generate a lot of random bytes. It is a good idea to perform\r\nsome other action (type on the keyboard, move the mouse, utilize the\r\ndisks) during the prime generation; this gives the random number\r\ngenerator a better chance to gain enough entropy.\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\ngpg-agent log\r\n2025-01-01 23:01:18 gpg-agent[681] DBG: chan_8 -> OK Pleased to meet you, process 731\r\n2025-01-01 23:01:21 gpg-agent[681] DBG: agent_cache_housekeeping\r\n2025-01-01 23:01:25 gpg-agent[681] DBG: agent_cache_housekeeping\r\n2025-01-01 23:01:29 gpg-agent[681] DBG: agent_cache_housekeeping\r\n2025-01-01 23:01:33 gpg-agent[681] DBG: agent_cache_housekeeping\r\n2025-01-01 23:01:37 gpg-agent[681] DBG: agent_cache_housekeeping\r\n2025-01-01 23:01:41 gpg-agent[681] DBG: agent_cache_housekeeping\r\n2025-01-01 23:01:45 gpg-agent[681] DBG: agent_cache_housekeeping\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\ngpg-agent.conf\r\n\r\nlog-file C:\\Temp\\gpg\\agent.log\r\nverbose\r\ndebug-level 1024\r\ndebug-quick-random\r\ndebug-pinentry\r\ndisable-scdaemon\r\n```\r\n\r\n - If the problem was occurring with a specific repository, can you provide the\r\n   URL to that repository to help us with testing?\r\n\r\nI asked a friend for help, but he was unable to reproduce the problem I was having. I guess maybe the environment is causing the problem, but I can't be sure.\r\n\r\nI've reproduced the problem in `cygwin`,`msys2` and `git bash`, and I'm not quite sure who to submit it to. Since it was first discovered in Git Bash, I chose to post it here. I didn't include the .gnupg folder because even after deleting the folder and letting gpg reinitialise, the problem persists. \r\n\r\nA friend of mine guessed that the TPM module was corrupted, I'm not sure if gpg uses that part.\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\nTpmPresent                : True\r\nTpmReady                  : True\r\nTpmEnabled                : True\r\nTpmActivated              : True\r\nTpmOwned                  : True\r\nRestartPending            : True\r\nManufacturerId            : 1095582720\r\nPpiVersion                : 1.3\r\nManufacturerIdTxt         : AMD\r\nManufacturerVersion       : 3.87.0.5\r\nManufacturerVersionFull20 : 3.87.0.5\r\nManagedAuthLevel          : Full\r\nOwnerAuth                 :\r\nOwnerClearDisabled        : False\r\nAutoProvisioning          : Enabled\r\nLockedOut                 : False\r\nLockoutHealTime           : 2 hours\r\nLockoutCount              : 0\r\nLockoutMax                : 32\r\nSelfTest                  : {}\r\n```\r\n\r\n`RestartPending` keeps true even after the restart. \r\n",
